.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
backend.hcl
*.tfvars.json

# emails.auto.tfvars holds personal addresses and this repo is public. It is the ONE input here
# that cannot be committed, and e2e_budget_alert_emails is now a REQUIRED variable so its absence
# fails loudly instead of silently unsubscribing the maintainer from their own cost alerts.
emails.auto.tfvars

# terraform.tfvars is committed HERE on purpose, overriding `**/terraform.tfvars` in
# infra/.gitignore and `infra/**/terraform.tfvars` in the root one — the negation has to live in
# this file because it is deeper than both. Only already-public values live in it. See README.md.
!terraform.tfvars
